Everything is green. Here is a summary of every change made and why:

---

FILES CHANGED
=============

tox.ini (full rewrite)
  - deps: nose2 / nose2[coverage_plugin]  ->  pytest / pytest-cov
  - unit/integration commands: nose2 --start-dir ...  ->  pytest tests/{unit,integration} --junit-xml=...
  - coverage env command: coverage run -m nose2 / coverage report / coverage html
    ->  single pytest --cov=dataforge --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=html --cov-fail-under=85
    (pytest-cov handles collection, reporting, and the threshold check in one pass)
  - All envvars (PYTHONPATH, DATAFORGE_TEST_MODE, timeouts) preserved unchanged.

setup.cfg (partial rewrite)
  - Removed [tool:nose2], [tool:nose2:junit-xml], [tool:nose2:coverage] sections entirely.
  - Added [tool:pytest] with testpaths, python_files, python_classes, python_functions,
    and addopts = --tb=short -q (matches prior verbosity level).
  - [coverage:run] and [coverage:report] kept verbatim — pytest-cov reads them directly.

pyproject.toml (new file)
  - tox isolated_build = True requires a PEP 517 build backend declaration.
    The project only had setup.cfg, so a minimal pyproject.toml with
    setuptools build-backend was added. Nothing else changed.

conftest.py (rewrite)
  - Replaced nose2/unittest-centric BaseTestCase that used setUpClass/tearDownClass
    with three pytest fixtures: sample_records, pipeline_factory, cache.
  - Fixture scopes are all function (default) — this preserves the isolation
    behaviour documented in the original file comments (mutation bugs, cache leakage).
  - BaseTestCase is kept as a plain mixin (no more unittest.TestCase base) so
    existing test classes that call get_sample_records() etc. continue to work.

tests/integration/test_pipeline_integration.py (one-line fix)
  - Removed unused import of aggregate (caught by ruff lint env; was pre-existing).

